{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815026-group-nouns","id":815026,"title":"Group nouns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-23T14:09:34-08:00","id":815026,"title":"Group nouns","content":"Ok! So, in the old world of darkness, we have:<br /> <br /> A Coterie of Vampires<br /> A Circle of Wraiths<br /> A Wu of Kuei-Jin<br /> A Cabal of Mages<br /> A Motley of Changelings<br /> A Pack of Garou<br /> <br /> Anyone know the other group names, for instance for Demon, other Fera, Mummy, Hunters, Ghouls, Dhampirs and Dhampyrs? Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 01-23-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:38:48-08:00","id":815041,"title":"","content":"Sabbat vampires also use the word pack instead of coterie. Similarly, the basic social unit of Technocrats is an <i>amalgam</i> instead of cabal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:02:26-08:00","id":815059,"title":"","content":"Some of the Fera:<br /> <br /> Cluster of Ananasi<br /> Clutch of Mokol\u00e9<br /> Nest of Nagah<br /> <i>Sentai</i> of Kitsune<br /> Slew of Rokea<br /> Sounder of Grondr<br /> <br /> Others, like the Bastet, are described as primarily solitary creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:05:59-08:00","id":815063,"title":"","content":"Parliament of Corax","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:11:27-08:00","id":815065,"title":"","content":"Isn't a parliament more like a Corax moot than a pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:29:23-08:00","id":815072,"title":"","content":"Demons, Mummies, Hunters, Ghouls, Dhampirs,and Dhampyrs, don't have any official terms for PC groups like this.<br /> <br /> Some Fera do, some don't (depending largely on their social organizations). Most are fairly individualistic and don't have formal groups. The Ratkin and Ajaba focus on larger groups (though Ratkin form smaller groups call packs to go on missions for a Colony). Simba have Prides unlike the other Bastet. Mokole, Nagah, and Rokea have the most direct analogs in Clutches, Nests, and Slews respectively.<br /> <br /> The Hengeyokai also use Sentai for their equivalent, which can include multiple Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:30:31-08:00","id":815075,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Parliaments aren't really good equivalents to packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T08:23:20-08:00","id":815471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815026-group-nouns#post815026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok! So, in the old world of darkness, we have:<br /> <br /> A Coterie of Vampires<br /> A Circle of Wraiths<br /> A Wu of Kuei-Jin<br /> A Cabal of Mages<br /> A Motley of Changelings<br /> A Pack of Garou<br /> <br /> Anyone know the other group names, for instance for Demon, other Fera, Mummy, Hunters, Ghouls, Dhampirs and Dhampyrs? Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>A Chimichanga of Mummies.<br /> A Konga of Hunters.<br /> A Bondage of Ghouls.<br /> A Dumpster of Dhampirs.<br /> A Hentai of Dhampyrs.<br /> A Heresy of Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 01-24-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:17:50-08:00","id":815650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815026-group-nouns?p=815041#post815041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sabbat vampires also use the word pack instead of coterie. Similarly, the basic social unit of Technocrats is an <i>amalgam</i> instead of cabal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From my Facebook post on the same question, someone answered:<br /> <br /> &gt;It'd be funny to see a Werewolf responding to a Craigslist ad about a Pack looking for a new member, and then showing up and it's just a bunch of vampire nationalists.<br /> &gt;<br /> &gt;&quot;Oh. Oh. Awkward. This is awkward.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:58:44-08:00","id":815672,"title":"","content":"Then the Garou tears through the Sabbat pack like a hot knife through butter? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:04:03-08:00","id":815676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815026-group-nouns?p=815471#post815471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dumpster of Dhampirs.<br /> A Hentai of Dhampyrs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, Dhampir vs. Dhampyr was always one of the most awkward distinctions in WoD -- on par with Demons and Daemons being different monsters in AD&amp;D. Sure, whatever you say, Gary.<br /> <br /> Is there a more appropriate Chinese or Japanese term for the offspring of a mortal and undead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:08:42-08:00","id":815914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/815026-group-nouns?p=815672#post815672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the Garou tears through the Sabbat pack like a hot knife through butter? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Numbers are unfortuntately the most powerful superweapon of all... If such a confrontation happened with humans (a numerically superior gang confronting an opponent that could put a few of them down with certainty in a fight) what would happen is a lot of posturing while the werewolf backed away, the Sabbat pack boasting about how they so could have taken it, if they had wanted to, it was so lucky they decided to let it go, while the werewolf growls that it could have killed any among them that tried - but ultimately leaving without confrontation.<br /> <br /> But add rage and beasts to the mix...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:31:14-08:00","id":816238,"title":"","content":"For feras: a yiff ball (sorry, had to)<br /> For hunters , a Party or MDG<br /> Demons: a Blasphemy or Legi\u00f3n <br /> For any Wyrm related : The Conga spiral of corruption","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}